.TH tkuimage n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuimage
.PP
Image helpers and a scrollable, zoomable viewer widget. Scaling uses the \fBimgtools\fR extension when it is installed and falls back to Tk's built\-in photo \fBsubsample\fR/\fBzoom\fR otherwise \-\- \fBimgtools\fR is optional (loaded via \fBcatch\fR).
.SS Helpers
.CS
tkuimage::fit imgW imgH boxW boxH ?mode?   ;# {newW newH scale}; mode contain|cover|none
tkuimage::load file ?dst?                  ;# photo from file (PNG/GIF native)
tkuimage::fromData bytes ?dst?             ;# photo from raw PNG/GIF bytes (in-memory)
tkuimage::scale src w h ?dst?              ;# scaled photo (imgtools or Tk fallback)
tkuimage::thumbnail src maxSize ?dst?      ;# contain-fit into maxSize box
.CE
.SS "Viewer widget"
.CS
set v [tkuimage::view .v ?-fitmode contain? ?-onchange cmd?]
pack $v -fill both -expand 1
tkuimage::openFile .v photo.png
tkuimage::zoomIn .v ; tkuimage::zoomOut .v ; tkuimage::zoom1 .v ; tkuimage::fitView .v
tkuimage::getImage  .v                      ;# the original photo image
tkuimage::zoomLevel .v                      ;# effective on-screen scale, 1.0 == 100%
.CE
.PP
The viewer is a frame with a scrolled canvas; in \fBcontain\fR fit\-mode it re\-fits on resize, otherwise it honours the current zoom. \fB\-onchange cmd\fR runs \fBcmd $path\fR after every redraw (load, zoom, fit, resize) \-\- useful to drive a status line; read the current scale with \fBzoomLevel\fR (returns the exact zoom factor in actual/zoom mode, the computed fit ratio in contain mode, or 0 before any load). Images are cleaned up automatically when the widget is destroyed. JPEG and other non\-native formats require the Img/tkimg extension for \fBload\fR/\fBopenFile\fR.
.SS "Changes in 0.2"
.IP \(bu
Added \fBzoomLevel\fR (effective on\-screen scale) and the \fBview \-onchange cmd\fR callback (fires after every redraw: load, zoom, fit, resize).
.IP \(bu
Fixed: switching to a smaller image now resizes the display so no pixels of the previous image remain.
.IP \(bu
Fixed: the first zoom out of fit\-mode continues from the on\-screen scale instead of jumping relative to the full original resolution.
.IP \(bu
imgtools is now detected lazily at scale time (used whenever available, regardless of package load order); display size is clamped to a sane range.
